        "original_id": "8c4a3b13-d454-5361-bb8f-1b07a9fdac59",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: René Clair, Emilio Fernández, Eugène Marin Labiche, Marc-Michel, Dolores del Río, Pedro Armendáriz\n- Works: The Italian Straw Hat, Bugambilia, Un chapeau de paille d'Italie\n- Roles: filmmaker, writer, film director, actor, screenwriter\n- Places: France, Mexico\n\nFacts:\n- René Clair was born René-Lucien Chomette on 11 November 1898 and was a French filmmaker and writer.\n- Emilio Fernández was born Emilio Fernández Romo on 26 March 1904 and was a Mexican film director, actor, and screenwriter.\n- The play Un chapeau de paille d'Italie was written in 1851 by Eugène Marin Labiche and Marc-Michel.\n- The Italian Straw Hat is a 1928 French silent film comedy written and directed by René Clair in his feature debut.\n- The Italian Straw Hat was based on the 1851 play Un chapeau de paille d'Italie.\n- Bugambilia is a 1945 Mexican film directed by Emilio Fernández and starring Dolores del Río and Pedro Armendáriz.\n- René Clair died on 15 March 1981.\n- Emilio Fernández died on 6 August 1986.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
